WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.730 --> 00:00:03.266
It is something that's kinda been lost.

00:00:03.266 --> 00:00:07.370
And it does make the elders happy
and excited that you're getting out there

00:00:07.370 --> 00:00:08.705
and doing what they used to do.

00:00:28.291 --> 00:00:30.093
Yeah, this is the end.

00:00:30.093 --> 00:00:31.427
End of the line right here.

00:00:39.402 --> 00:00:41.104
The fish are all spawned up now.

00:00:41.104 --> 00:00:42.939
These are uh, sockeye salmon.

00:00:42.939 --> 00:00:45.708
Some of them are still spawning,
you can see eggs and stuff in the water,

00:00:45.708 --> 00:00:48.978
but the fish are kinda like this
all over the place up here right now.

00:00:50.980 --> 00:00:53.182
I mean they’re in the lake,
they’re in the creeks.

00:00:53.182 --> 00:00:54.484
I mean they're everywhere.

00:00:55.018 --> 00:00:58.788
You gotta catch them as soon as they get
into the lake basically cause once,

00:00:58.788 --> 00:01:03.059
they hit fresh water, they stop feeding
and then they start basically dying.

00:01:04.394 --> 00:01:06.062
They start turning red
and their meat starts

00:01:06.062 --> 00:01:09.232
to turn white,
and they no longer taste good at all.

00:01:09.232 --> 00:01:11.501
And it's like mushy. It's like soft.

00:01:11.501 --> 00:01:12.535
They're not good to eat.

00:01:12.769 --> 00:01:15.438
For the next couple weeks, they’ll
be fish around just kinda

00:01:15.438 --> 00:01:17.040
dying and floating up on the beach.

00:01:18.675 --> 00:01:20.443
Can tell that the bears have been coming down

00:01:20.443 --> 00:01:24.947
because all the, all the grass is all matted down
and there's dead fish all over the place.

00:01:25.615 --> 00:01:28.885
This is kinda their feeding ground.

00:01:28.885 --> 00:01:30.319
Let's see what else I can see.

00:01:35.458 --> 00:01:36.592
Oh man, look at that.

00:01:36.592 --> 00:01:38.461
The bears stashing his fish right here.

00:01:38.461 --> 00:01:39.762
It's super fresh too.

00:01:39.762 --> 00:01:44.267
And once the bears get full, they’ll
kinda stop eating the whole salmon.

00:01:44.300 --> 00:01:47.003
They’ll just start eating like
the good parts, like the belly and stuff.

00:01:47.537 --> 00:01:49.138
Think
I'm gonna keep going a little more.

00:01:49.138 --> 00:01:51.741
Do a little more exploring. That's a pretty cool find.

00:01:53.109 --> 00:01:55.111
It's good just to get out and explore.

00:01:55.378 --> 00:01:57.080
Stuff's kinda always changing out here too
you know.

00:01:57.080 --> 00:02:01.384
The topography of the land and it's
good to see if the salmon are schooling up

00:02:01.384 --> 00:02:02.685
in different places.

00:02:02.685 --> 00:02:04.887
How many bears are out and about.

00:02:04.887 --> 00:02:07.056
You know, what all the animals
are up to this time of the year. I’m

00:02:08.591 --> 00:02:10.960
back here just kinda checking out
where the bears are hanging out.

00:02:11.227 --> 00:02:13.529
Where they're at
and about how many there are around.

00:02:14.297 --> 00:02:16.332
I mean, there's
there's a lot of bears around here

00:02:16.566 --> 00:02:19.368
and they will try to protect
their feeding ground.

00:02:19.569 --> 00:02:20.837
That is something you kinda have to

00:02:20.837 --> 00:02:23.206
worry about cause we're like right
where they’re eating right now.

00:02:25.041 --> 00:02:27.610
I like kinda knowing what they're doing,
where they’re at.

00:02:27.610 --> 00:02:29.679
Partially just so you can stay away
from them kind of a thing.

00:02:29.946 --> 00:02:32.348
Cause certain years
you'll have more aggressive bears.

00:02:32.348 --> 00:02:35.151
Some years
you'll have bears that break into stuff.

00:02:35.218 --> 00:02:35.651
But there is that off

00:02:35.651 --> 00:02:39.655
chance that you run into that bear
that just wants to eat your face off.

00:02:40.623 --> 00:02:43.626
I can hear the bears move around in here
but I can't see ‘em.

00:02:43.893 --> 00:02:45.495
I don't like being this low to ‘em.

00:02:45.495 --> 00:02:48.698
I’m gonna climb up this hill up here
so I can kinda see what's going on.

00:02:50.133 --> 00:02:51.400
Don’t have to have a showdown with a bear.

00:02:51.400 --> 00:02:52.301
If I don't have to.

00:02:56.038 --> 00:02:57.473
if I don’t have to.
Oh (bleep), that’s a brown bear!

00:02:58.875 --> 00:03:00.009
He’s a pretty big bear

00:03:03.312 --> 00:03:04.447
growing up out here.

00:03:04.447 --> 00:03:07.617
It's burned in to you that you shouldn't
really be afraid of them.

00:03:08.351 --> 00:03:09.619
I mean, you should respect them.

00:03:09.619 --> 00:03:10.887
But if they do just want to leave

00:03:10.887 --> 00:03:12.255
you alone, for the most part,

00:03:14.423 --> 00:03:16.459
three bears just came out of the woods.

00:03:16.859 --> 00:03:18.594
They’re fighting over a fishing spot.

00:03:19.195 --> 00:03:20.630
They're a pretty good size too.

00:03:20.863 --> 00:03:23.132
They're coming to check out the salmon
in that creek.

00:03:23.533 --> 00:03:26.469
I’m not really worried about the bears,
partially because I have a gun.

00:03:26.869 --> 00:03:28.504
They don't really care about you.

00:03:28.504 --> 00:03:31.307
Especially right now cause they have like
as much food as they can eat.

00:03:33.543 --> 00:03:36.312
This time of year, you can really see
the life cycle of everything.

00:03:36.479 --> 00:03:37.680
You know cause the fish are coming

00:03:37.680 --> 00:03:40.750
up and everything
kinda seems to feed off the fish somewhat.

00:03:41.617 --> 00:03:43.619
There’s just thousands of fish out here.

00:03:43.619 --> 00:03:45.421
The seals are coming in to eat the salmon.

00:03:45.421 --> 00:03:46.656
I mean the bears are here.

00:03:48.758 --> 00:03:51.627
Be nice if I can get out,
catch some pike and maybe shoot a seal

00:03:53.162 --> 00:03:54.363
You know, have a little variety.

